{% set local_problem %}
<p>Many <a href="/recent-projects/">Somerville homes</a> are older properties that have weathered decades of Alabama's humidity. When gutters have been neglected over the years, fascia boards take the damage. Water running behind gutters soaks into the wood, creating conditions for rot, mold, and insect damage.</p>

<p>Fascia problems are common in older rural homes — and commonly missed. Homeowners call about gutter issues and we find the real problem is the rotted wood behind the gutters.</p>

<p>Caught early, fascia repair is straightforward. Left alone, rot spreads to rafters and roof structure.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>We start with a thorough inspection for water damage, soft spots, and rot. For damaged sections, we remove gutters, cut out rotted wood, and install new fascia boards using quality materials designed for our humid climate.</p>

<p>Then we install seamless gutters designed to prevent the overflow that caused the rot.</p>
{% endset %}

